  recipeId: assembly
  concept: 'Authored objective: Commission the protected board.

    Authored requirement:
    Fit W035, enable the protected virtual bench, record live 3.3 V and feedback,
    and qualify a fresh load-current sample.

    General teaching principle: Assembly
    should follow the authored parts and connections and be validated with the game''s
    authoritative inspection or objective checks.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: Following an assembly plan prevents a plausible-looking but incorrectly
    connected build.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A visually complete assembly is not proof of every required terminal,
    orientation or inspection check.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Commission the protected board\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Commission the protected board\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 94, perform the objective \u2018Commission the protected board\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Fit W035, enable
    the protected virtual bench, record live 3.3 V and feedback, and qualify a fresh
    load-current sample.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial
    does not grade your answer."
